  ($q$alg-428$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Linear inequalities in two variables$q$, 2, null, $q$Which ordered pair (x, y) is a solution to the inequality 2x + 4y < 13?$q$, $q$["(5, 5)","(2, 1)","(2, 6)","(7, 2)"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$Substituting (2, 1) gives 8 < 13, which is true. Each other pair gives a value of at least 13.$q$),
  ($q$alg-429$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Linear inequalities in one variable$q$, 1, null, $q$What is the smallest integer x that satisfies 4x − 2 > 22?$q$, $q$["8","6","24","7"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$4x > 24 → x > 6, so the smallest integer is 7.$q$),
