  ($q$alg-431$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Linear functions$q$, 2, null, $q$The linear function f satisfies f(3) = 18 and f(4) = 23. What is the value of f(9)?$q$, $q$["53","43","48","28"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$Slope = (23 − 18)/(4 − 3) = 5. Then f(9) = 23 + 5(9 − 4) = 48.$q$),
  ($q$alg-432$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Word problems$q$, 2, null, $q$Gym A charges a $25 sign-up fee plus $3 per visit. Gym B charges a $9 sign-up fee plus $5 per visit. After how many visits is the total cost the same at both gyms?$q$, $q$["8","9","16","7"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$25 + 3v = 9 + 5v → 16 = 2v → v = 8.$q$),
  ($q$alg-433$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Linear inequalities in two variables$q$, 2, null, $q$A school club has $72 to spend on posters and banners. Posters cost $3 each and banners cost $5 each. If the club buys 2 banners, what is the maximum number of posters it can buy?$q$, $q$["22","24","20","21"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$3p + 5(2) ≤ 72 → 3p ≤ 62 → p ≤ 62/3, so at most 20 posters.$q$),
  ($q$alg-434$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Systems of two linear equations$q$, 2, null, $q$2x + 5y = 2
