In the given system, k is a constant. The system has infinitely many solutions. What is the value of k?$q$, $q$["8","7","6","2"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$The coefficient rows are proportional with factor 4, so the equations describe the same line only if k = 4·2 = 8.$q$),
  ($q$alg-435$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Systems of two linear equations$q$, 2, null, $q$A theater sold 56 tickets for a total of $735. Adult tickets cost $18 and child tickets cost $11. How many adult tickets were sold?$q$, $q$["39","38","17","20"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$Let a be adult tickets and c child tickets: a + c = 56 and 18a + 11c = 735. Substituting c = 56 − a gives 7a = 119, so a = 17.$q$),
  ($q$alg-436$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Word problems$q$, 2, null, $q$One machine fills 5 boxes per hour and another fills 8 boxes per hour. Working together, how many hours will they need to fill 39 boxes?$q$, $q$["26","7","3","4"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$Together they fill 5 + 8 = 13 boxes per hour, so 39 boxes take 39/13 = 3 hours.$q$),
  ($q$alg-437$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Linear equations in two variables$q$, 1, null, $q$What is the x-intercept of the graph of 8x − 3y = −8 in the xy-plane?$q$, $q$["(−8, 0)","(−1, 0)","(1, 0)","(0, 8/3)"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$The x-intercept occurs where y = 0: 8x = −8, so x = −1. The point is (−1, 0).$q$),
