In the given system of equations, k is a constant. If the system has infinitely many solutions, what is the value of k?$q$, $q$["20","8","24","2"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$The second equation must be 4 times the first: 4(2x + 5y) = 24. Matching the x-coefficients gives k = 8.$q$),
  ($q$alg-440$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Linear equations in one variable$q$, 1, null, $q$If 5(x + 2) = −x − 8, what is the value of x?$q$, $q$["−3","4","3","−1"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Distribute: 5x + 10 = −x − 8. Collect x-terms on the left and constants on the right: 6x = −18. So x = −3.$q$),
  ($q$alg-441$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Linear inequalities in two variables$q$, 2, null, $q$A school club has $81 to spend on posters and banners. Posters cost $4 each and banners cost $6 each. If the club buys 4 banners, what is the maximum number of posters it can buy?$q$, $q$["18","14","20","15"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$4p + 6(4) ≤ 81 → 4p ≤ 57 → p ≤ 57/4, so at most 14 posters.$q$),
  ($q$alg-442$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Systems of two linear equations$q$, 1, null, $q$If 3x + 2y = 15 and 4x + 2y = 18, what is the value of x + y?$q$, $q$["−3","3","6","0"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$Solving the system by elimination gives x = 3 and y = 3, so x + y = 6.$q$),
  ($q$alg-443$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Linear inequalities in one variable$q$, 1, null, $q$How many integers x satisfy 10 < 4x + 2 ≤ 58?$q$, $q$["12","13","14","11"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Subtract 2 and divide by 4: 2 < x ≤ 14. The integers are 3 through 14, which is 12 integers.$q$),
