  ($q$alg-445$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Linear inequalities in two variables$q$, 2, null, $q$Which ordered pair (x, y) is a solution to the inequality 4x + 4y < 10?$q$, $q$["(0, 1)","(6, 1)","(3, 0)","(3, 4)"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Substituting (0, 1) gives 4 < 10, which is true. Each other pair gives a value of at least 10.$q$),
  ($q$alg-446$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Linear inequalities in one variable$q$, 1, null, $q$What is the smallest integer x that satisfies 5x − 11 > −9?$q$, $q$["−1","1","2","0"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$5x > 2 → x > 2/5, so the smallest integer is 1.$q$),
  ($q$alg-447$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Linear functions$q$, 2, null, $q$Line ℓ has slope −3/2. Line m is perpendicular to ℓ and passes through the point (4, 2). What is the y-intercept of line m?$q$, $q$["14/3","2/3","8","−2/3"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$The slope of m is the negative reciprocal, 2/3. Then b = y − mx = 2 − (2/3)(4) = −2/3.$q$),
