  ($q$alg-450$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Linear functions$q$, 2, null, $q$Line ℓ has slope −3/2. Line m is perpendicular to ℓ and passes through the point (5, −3). What is the y-intercept of line m?$q$, $q$["19/3","1/3","−19/3","9/2"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$The slope of m is the negative reciprocal, 2/3. Then b = y − mx = −3 − (2/3)(5) = −19/3.$q$),
