  ($q$alg-452$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Linear equations in two variables$q$, 2, null, $q$In the xy-plane, a line is given by 6x − 5y = −28. What is the slope of the line?$q$, $q$["−5/6","28/5","−6/5","6/5"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$Solve for y: −5y = −6x − 28. Dividing every term by −5 gives y = 6/5x + 28/5, so the slope is 6/5.$q$),
