  ($q$alg-457$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Linear functions$q$, 2, null, $q$The linear function f satisfies f(0) = −8 and f(1) = −2. What is the value of f(2)?$q$, $q$["10","−2","−1","4"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$Slope = (−2 − (−8))/(1 − 0) = 6. Then f(2) = −2 + 6(2 − 1) = 4.$q$),
  ($q$alg-458$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Systems of two linear equations$q$, 1, null, $q$If x + 2y = 13 and 4x − 4y = 16, what is the value of y?$q$, $q$["−3","3","7","4"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$Eliminating x (or substituting) from the two equations gives y = 3 (and x = 7); check: (7) + 2(3) = 13.$q$),
  ($q$alg-459$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Systems of two linear equations$q$, 2, null, $q$A theater sold 35 tickets for a total of $295. Adult tickets cost $12 and child tickets cost $7. How many adult tickets were sold?$q$, $q$["25","10","23","13"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$Let a be adult tickets and c child tickets: a + c = 35 and 12a + 7c = 295. Substituting c = 35 − a gives 5a = 50, so a = 10.$q$),
