  ($q$alg-462$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Linear equations in two variables$q$, 2, null, $q$A line in the xy-plane is given by y = −x − 7. If the point (−2, k) lies on the line, what is the value of k?$q$, $q$["−5","5","−6","−9"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Substitute x = −2: k = −(−2) − 7 = −5.$q$),
