  ($q$alg-467$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Linear equations in one variable$q$, 2, null, $q$For constants b and c, the equation 7(bx + c) = −14x + 21 is true for all values of x. What is the value of b + c?$q$, $q$["7","8","1","−5"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$For the equation to hold for every x, coefficients must match: 7b = −14 → b = −2, and 7c = 21 → c = 3. So b + c = 1.$q$),
