  ($q$alg-472$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Linear equations in two variables$q$, 2, null, $q$In the xy-plane, a line is given by 4x − 3y = −7. What is the slope of the line?$q$, $q$["−4/3","4/3","7/3","−3/4"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$Solve for y: −3y = −4x − 7. Dividing every term by −3 gives y = 4/3x + 7/3, so the slope is 4/3.$q$),
