  ($q$alg-480$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Linear equations in two variables$q$, 2, null, $q$The equation C = 17 + 13h gives the total cost C, in dollars, of renting a kayak for h hours, including a fixed fee. What does 13 represent in this context?$q$, $q$["The number of hours rented","The total cost of the rental","The cost for each additional hour of rental","The fixed fee for the rental"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$In C = 17 + 13h, 13 is the coefficient of h, so it is the rate of change: the cost per hour. The constant 17 is the fixed fee.$q$),
