  ($q$alg-507$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Linear equations in two variables$q$, 2, null, $q$The equation T = 51 + 6d models the total number of pages T that a student has read after d days of reading. What does 51 represent in this context?$q$, $q$["The number of days spent reading","The total number of pages read after d days","The number of pages the student had read before the first day","The number of pages read each day"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$In T = 51 + 6d, 51 is the value of T when d = 0, i.e., the pages already read at the start. The 6 is the pages per day.$q$),
