  ($q$alg-516$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Systems of two linear equations$q$, 2, null, $q$The system of equations 2x + 3y = 4 and kx + 12y = 13 has no solution. What is the value of k?$q$, $q$["9","2","8","4"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$For no solution the lines must be parallel but distinct: the coefficients must be proportional. Multiplying the first equation by 4 gives 8x + 12y = 16; since the constants differ (16 ≠ 13), k = 8 gives no solution.$q$),
