  ($q$alg-522$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Systems of two linear equations$q$, 2, null, $q$The system of equations 4x + 3y = 8 and kx + 9y = 22 has no solution. What is the value of k?$q$, $q$["12","3","4","13"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$For no solution the lines must be parallel but distinct: the coefficients must be proportional. Multiplying the first equation by 3 gives 12x + 9y = 24; since the constants differ (24 ≠ 22), k = 12 gives no solution.$q$),
