  ($q$alg-538$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Linear functions$q$, 2, null, $q$Line ℓ is perpendicular to the line y = 2x + 1 and passes through the point (4, −1). What is the slope of line ℓ?$q$, $q$["−2","−1/2","2","1/2"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$Perpendicular lines have slopes that are negative reciprocals. The given slope is 2, so ℓ has slope −1/2. The point does not change the slope.$q$),
