  ($q$alg-586$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Linear functions$q$, 2, null, $q$The function f is linear. If f(2) = −13 and f(4) = −17, what is the value of f(−3)?$q$, $q$["−1","−5","6","−3"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$The slope is (−17 − (−13))/(4 − 2) = −2, and f(0) = −9. So f(−3) = −2(−3) − 9 = −3.$q$),
