  ($q$alg-598$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Systems of two linear equations$q$, 2, null, $q$2x + 6y = 13 kx + 6y = 22 In the system above, k is a constant. For what value of k does the system have no solution?$q$, $q$["2","6","4","3"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$No solution requires parallel lines: the ratios of x- and y-coefficients match but the constants do not. k/2 = 6/6, so k = 2. (The constants 13 and 22 are not in that same ratio, so the lines are distinct.)$q$),
  ($q$alg-599$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Linear functions$q$, 2, null, $q$A line has slope 6 and passes through the point (−1, 24). At what x-value does the line cross the x-axis?$q$, $q$["−5","−4","−1","−6"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$y = 6(x − (−1)) + 24. Setting y = 0 gives x − (−1) = −4, so x = −5.$q$),
