  ($q$alg-603$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Linear equations in two variables$q$, 2, null, $q$The line with equation −4x + 18y = −36 crosses the x-axis at (p, 0) and the y-axis at (0, q). What is the value of p + q?$q$, $q$["14","7","11","−7"]$q$::jsonb, 1, $q$Setting y = 0 gives p = 9. Setting x = 0 gives q = −2. So p + q = 7.$q$),
