  ($q$alg-606$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Word problems$q$, 2, null, $q$A taxi company charges $5.00 for the first mile and $3.50 for each additional mile. A passenger paid $40.00 for a ride. How many miles was the ride? (Assume the ride covered a whole number of miles.)$q$, $q$["12","9","11","10"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$The first mile costs $5.00, leaving $40.00 − $5.00 = $35.00 for additional miles: 10 additional miles at $3.50. Total distance = 1 + 10 = 11 miles.$q$),
